      "reasoning": "Let x be the rectangle width along BC and y its height along AB. Since D lies on hypotenuse AC, similar triangles give x/β + y/α = 1. Thus A=xy=αx(1−x/β), a concave quadratic with its unique maximum at x=β/2; then y=α/2 and Amax=αβ/4. The two roots are α=(5−√13)/2 and β=(5+√13)/2, so αβ=3 and Amax=3/4, which is the third choice."
